      "bibo:abstract": {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The world of digital data is full of unknown data, with are not FAIR (Findable, Accessible, Interoperable and Reusable).\nThis modern species of dragons on a (digital) map of the internet as sign for unknown and dangerous areas, the unknown\ndigital data dragons, have to be resolved by digital techniques. We could use the Semantic Web and all of its ideas for this\nchallenge. This paper focuses on data dragons in the humanities domain, especially in archaeology and proposes ideas to\novercome the data dragons to achieve FAIR LOUD in archaeology!"
      },
      "bibo:authorList": {
        "@id": "https://w3id.org/squirrelpapers/v1/i1/e1#authors"
      },
